#Donor/acceptor classification for the dynamic hydrogen-bond mechanism,
#keyed by amber.grp's renamed particle types (e.g. ALA:N -> AN) instead of
#plain PDB atom names -- companion table to amber.grp/amber.ff, generated
#by cross-referencing amber.grp against ProteinDonorAcceptor.hbond (same
#classification, see that file's header for the rationale and sources).
#
#Use this table (via hbond.path in the .msp file) when the topology was
#built with --grp amber.grp --ff amber.ff (--rigidbody or otherwise): those
#options rename every particle, so ProteinDonorAcceptor.hbond's plain
#atom-name keys ("N", "O", ...) would no longer match. Residue name is kept
#as the first column even though amber's renamed types are already globally
#unique on their own, for a uniform 4-column format across both tables.
#
#Format: <resname> <type> <donor> <acceptor>, donor/acceptor are 0 or 1.
#
#The sixth column is a SECOND antecedent: a backbone amide nitrogen is planar
#between CA and the previous residue's C, and its hydrogen points opposite
#their bisector. CA alone is 58 degrees off and costs a factor 3.2 on
#cos^2(theta) -- see ProteinDonorAcceptor.hbond for the measurement. "-C" is
#the previous residue's C, resolved on the plain atom name because its type
#depends on that residue.

ACE  XO    0 2 XC

ALA  AN    1 0 ACA -C
ALA  AO    0 2 AC

ARG  RN    1 0 RCA -C
ARG  RO    0 2 RC
ARG  RNE   1 0 RCD
ARG  RNH1  2 0 RCZ
ARG  RNH2  2 0 RCZ

ASN  NN    1 0 NCA -C
ASN  NO    0 2 NC
ASN  NND2  2 0 NCG
ASN  NOD1  0 2 NCG

ASP  DN    1 0 DCA -C
ASP  DO    0 2 DC
ASP  DOD1  0 2 DCG
ASP  DOD2  0 2 DCG

CYS  CN    1 0 CCA -C
CYS  CO    0 2 CC
CYS  CSG   1 1 CCB

GLN  QN    1 0 QCA -C
GLN  QO    0 2 QC
GLN  QNE2  2 0 QCD
GLN  QOE1  0 2 QCD

GLU  EN    1 0 ECA -C
GLU  EO    0 2 EC
GLU  EOE1  0 2 ECD
GLU  EOE2  0 2 ECD

GLY  GN    1 0 GCA -C
GLY  GO    0 2 GC

HIS  HN    1 0 HCA -C
HIS  HO    0 2 HC
HIS  HND1  1 1 HCE1
HIS  HNE2  1 1 HCE1

ILE  IN    1 0 ICA -C
ILE  IO    0 2 IC

LEU  LN    1 0 LCA -C
LEU  LO    0 2 LC

LYS  KN    1 0 KCA -C
LYS  KO    0 2 KC
LYS  KNZ   3 0 KCE

MET  MN    1 0 MCA -C
MET  MO    0 2 MC

NME  ZN    1 0 ZC

PHE  FN    1 0 FCA -C
PHE  FO    0 2 FC

PRO  PO    0 2 PC

SER  SN    1 0 SCA -C
SER  SO    0 2 SC
SER  SOG   1 2 SCB

THR  TN    1 0 TCA -C
THR  TO    0 2 TC
THR  TOG1  1 2 TCB

TRP  WN    1 0 WCA -C
TRP  WO    0 2 WC
TRP  WNE1  1 0 WCD1

TYR  YN    1 0 YCA -C
TYR  YO    0 2 YC
TYR  YOH   1 2 YCZ

VAL  VN    1 0 VCA -C
VAL  VO    0 2 VC
